  "trends": "AI development and deployment hubs. Here is what the data shows, and what it means for businesses making decisions about AI investment right now.India's AI Market is Growing Faster Than Almost Any Other EconomyIndia's AI market was valued at $7.63 billion in 2024 and is projected to reach $122.32 billion by 2035 - a CAGR of 42.2%. North India, led by Delhi NCR, holds a 30% share of India's AI market. The concentration of enterprise IT, government institutions, and financial services in the NCR makes it the natural centre of AI adoption in the country's northern economy.Delhi NCR is Becoming a Governance and Fintech AI ClusterDelhi NCR is specifically identified as a major AI-driven governance and financial technology cluster in multiple industry analyses. The proximity to central government institutions - DPIIT, SEBI, RBI regional offices, NIC, and the NIELIT Delhi IndiaAI Data Lab - creates both demand for GovTech AI and an environment of regulatory influence that shapes how AI is deployed across the private sector.The IndiaAI Mission is Creating Real InfrastructureThe Indian government's IndiaAI Mission funds shared compute platforms, Centres of Excellence in healthcare, agriculture, and sustainable cities in New Delhi, and a new Centre of Excellence for AI in education with a Rs 500 crore outlay announced in Budget 2025. BharatGen - the world's first government-funded multimodal LLM initiative - was launched in Delhi in 2024. Businesses building AI systems now are building on top of improving national AI infrastructure.80% of Indian Companies Have Made AI a Core Strategic PriorityAccording to BCG, 80% of Indian companies consider AI a core strategic priority - above the global average of 75%. In Delhi NCR's enterprise and startup environment, this translates to real procurement decisions and real competition. The businesses that have already built functional AI systems are pulling ahead, particularly in customer experience, cost efficiency, and compliance automation.India Ranks First Globally in AI Skill PenetrationAccording to the Stanford AI Index 2024, India ranks first in the world for AI skill penetration, with Delhi NCR housing significant AI talent through IIT Delhi, JNU, IIIT Delhi, Jawaharlal Nehru University's computational labs, and a dense cluster of AI-focused companies. Despite this talent concentration, building and retaining an in-house AI team in Delhi is expensive and slow - which is why working with a specialist AI development partner often makes more business sense than hiring from scratch.The DPDP Act Changes the Rules for AI Data HandlingIndia's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 fundamentally changes how businesses must handle personal data in AI systems. For any system that processes user queries, customer profiles, or employee records, DPDP Act compliance is non-negotiable. This is not a future concern - enforcement is underway. AI systems built without data governance controls face real legal and reputational exposure.  OUR AI DEVELOPMENT PROCESS",
